// THE SHADOWS' TRANSMITTANCE (PHOTON-7 10-4 R8; L9: the sun and the lamps follow the ray through glass, attenuated by its
// material). A PANE (a surface that blends with what is behind it: Fade, Transparent, Refractive under alpha 1 -
// OgreScene's paneTransmittance) occludes no light: it is in no depth map, and casts only into the shadow node's
// TRANSMITTANCE LAYER, atlasT (OgreShadow.cpp: R8, the depth atlas's own layout, cleared to 1, built only while a drawn
// scene holds a pane), each map's pane pass testing that map's opaque depth read-only - so a pane behind the nearest
// opaque caster is not between the light and its receiver - and multiplying the layer by its 1 - alpha (the caster's
// blendblock: dest x src; no depth write). NEUTRAL, by Ogre's own glass model: Ogre's blend passes 1 - alpha whatever the
// colour (a tinted, RGB transmittance is on the owner's review list).
//
// (1) THE WRITER: a pane caster's pixel in a pass with a colour target (the layer's) writes its transmittance - ONE
//     shader for every alpha (the one read's F12: the value rode the permutation, and an alpha drag compiled up to 255
//     caster PSOs with the shadow missing while each built): `jah_pane_caster` 1 (ScenePbs::calculateHashForPreCaster)
//     reads its material's 1 - alpha in the vertex stage (ScenePbs::fillBuffersForV2 binds the material buffer for a
//     pane's caster) and hands it flat to the pixel; 2 an Additive, which passes everything (1). After DoShadowCastPS,
//     over the depth it wrote into the colour output.
// (2) THE READER: every shadow lookup of a shadowed colour pass (`jah_shadow_transmit`, the listener's: OgreFog.cpp;
//     a node without the layer binds a white texel, so the permutation never depends on whether a pane was drawn) is
//     multiplied by the layer at the lookup's own uv - one bilinear read where the depth is
//     PCF-filtered - inside the fork's getShadow / getShadowPoint (custom_shadow_transmit_uv / custom_shadow_transmit),
//     before the map rectangle's clamp, so a lookup outside its map stays lit.
// THE AT-SIGN RULE: no directive mark in any comment of this file.

@property( hlms_shadowcaster && jah_pane_caster && !hlms_render_depth_only )
@piece( custom_ps_posExecution )
	@property( jah_pane_caster == 2 )
		outColour = 1.0;
	@else
		outColour = inPs.jahPaneT;
	@end
@end
@end
// (its vertex stage's pieces - the material's declaration, the value, the flat interpolant - are in a file both stages
// read: JahFog_piece_vs_piece_ps.any, beside the hooks they ride)

@property( jah_shadow_transmit && !hlms_shadowcaster )
@piece( custom_shadow_transmit_uv )
	float2 jahShadowTransmitUv = uv;
@end
@piece( custom_shadow_transmit )
	retVal *= midf_c( OGRE_SampleLevel( jahShadowTransmit, jahShadowTransmitSampler, jahShadowTransmitUv, 0.0 ).x );
@end
@end
